Remotely Save Lite
Copyright 2026 stdlo

This product is a fork of Remotely Save
(https://github.com/remotely-save/remotely-save), by fyears and its
contributors, released under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It was
taken from version 0.5.25 (commit 34db181).

What this fork changed:

- Removed the source-available `pro/` folder and everything that used
  it: the paid account, Smart Conflict, file content history, and the
  paid backends.
- Restored the sync engine (`src/sync.ts`) from upstream's
  Apache-2.0 history, before it moved into `pro/`, without its paid
  hooks.
- Kept only the Dropbox backend; removed S3, WebDAV, Webdis, and
  OneDrive.
- Gave the plugin its own id, name, database, protocol actions, and
  Dropbox redirect, so it installs beside upstream.
- Replaced Biome with oxlint and oxfmt, and added tests for the sync
  plan decisions.

Each changed source file says what changed in a comment at its top.
